// GENERATED by make_system_health.py -- edit the generator, not this file.
//
//  THE BANNER CONTRACT.  Asked for by the operator 2026-08-26: a warning area on
//  every page, shown ONLY when there is a real message -- 'just say system ok is
//  useless and wastes screen estate'.
//
//  ONE line carries EVERY subsystem, priority-ordered.  If each subsystem got its
//  own banner, every page would carry three conditional lines within a season.
//
//  🚨 SEEDED AND restoreOnStartup ON PURPOSE, AND THIS IS NOT COSMETIC.
//  Basic UI visibility=[X==ON] matches NEITHER ==ON nor ==OFF when X is NULL.
//  That is what made set_ON_OFF render nothing but separator lines in August.
//  For an ordinary widget a NULL fails loud; for a WARNING banner it FAILS
//  SILENT -- the line that should appear when something is wrong hides itself
//  because its own Item was never written.  So: seeded at startup, restored on
//  startup, and rewritten on every tick whether or not anything changed.
//
//  The gate is a Switch, not a test on the text being empty: string comparison in
//  Basic UI visibility is unproven in this config and a banner is not the place
//  to discover it.

Switch systemWarningActive "Има предупреждение [%s]"  (gPersist_On_Every_Change)
String systemWarningText   "[%s]"                     (gPersist_On_Every_Change)
